{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual input-to-output skip helps conv-heavy cells but badly hurts cells whose other edges are all skip or pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "A conv on edge 3 is hugely beneficial when the cell lacks convs elsewhere but redundant and harmful once the node-1 path already has a 3x3 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 1 receives no input, a conv on edge 4 processes zeros and contributes nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting edge 0 when edge 1 is also absent severs node 2's input as well, collapsing the deep path."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 2 does not feed the output, removing its input edge is nearly harmless."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "A conv on edge 5 adds less when node 2 has impoverished input from node 0."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with skip loses capacity, while replacing none or pooling is neutral or positive."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for a 1x1 is a slight downgrade, whereas upgrading from skip, pool or none gives large gains."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is already absent removes one of the few remaining routes to the 